{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0007","statement":"The Battle of Fredericksburg was fought December 11–15, 1862, in and around Fredericksburg, Virginia.","source_span":"The Battle of Fredericksburg was fought December 11–15, 1862, in and around Fredericksburg, Virginia"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0007","statement":"The battle was fought between General Robert E. Lee's Confederate Army of Northern Virginia and the Union Army of the Potomac.","source_span":"between General Robert E. Lee's Confederate Army of Northern Virginia and the Union Army of the Potomac"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0007","statement":"The Union Army of the Potomac was commanded by Maj. Gen. Ambrose E. Burnside.","source_span":"commanded by Maj. Gen. Ambrose E. Burnside"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0007","statement":"The Union army's frontal assaults against entrenched Confederate defenders occurred on December 13.","source_span":"The Union army's futile frontal assaults on December 13 against entrenched Confederate defenders"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0007","statement":"Union casualties at Fredericksburg were more than twice as heavy as Confederate casualties.","source_span":"Union casualties more than twice as heavy as those suffered by the Confederates"}
